WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.336
-Welcome back. The one and only
Elton John is joining us.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.503
We love you!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:06.606
The new album,
"The Lockdown Sessions,"

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.441
is out now.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.942
Did you ever think

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:14.614
such a shy child would end up
being you, Elton John?

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.449
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:18.451
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.319
Never in a million years
could I have expected

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:22.154
what's happened to me
in my lifetime, Jimmy.

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:23.523
-Really?

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:28.494
-The fact that I was a child
and I was a very shy child

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:30.630
when I started playing
the piano, and it's all

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.465
down to Jerry Lee Lewis
and Little Richard.

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:35.635
When they started jumping up and
down and playing it standing up,

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.971
then that changed my whole life
completely.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:41.407
And that's what I wanted to do
and I wanted to make music.

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:43.576
I didn't ever intend
to become Elton John.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.912
I just wanted to be involved
in music and play it.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:50.082
And I got gratification from
that and love from doing that.

00:00:50.082 --> 00:00:51.751
-Yeah.
-And so, I thought, yeah.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.119
This is -- I like this.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.788
-Yeah, well, you did it better
than most people.

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:58.958
I want to say, your "Farewell
Yellow Brick Road Tour,"

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.960
I was ready to go see you.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.462
'cause this is
your farewell tour.

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.864
It got cut short
because of the pandemic,

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:08.034
and also maybe a sign that we
don't want you to say farewell.

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:10.370
[ Cheers and applause ]
We want you to keep going.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.038
Don't stop!

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:15.041
But you're coming back.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:17.376
-Yeah, I'm coming back
to New Orleans in January.

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:20.813
I've just had my hip replaced,
on the right leg.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.316
So I'm rehabbing in London
at the moment.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.918
And it's all going well,
and I just wanted to make sure

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:27.753
that I could actually
get through the whole tour.

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:29.188
Because before the operation,

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:30.690
I don't think
I would have been able to.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.524
So, we pushed some dates back,

00:01:32.524 --> 00:01:34.026
and I start again
in New Orleans.

00:01:34.026 --> 00:01:36.028
And I cannot wait,
because we were here,

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:37.897
we were roaring
like an express train.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.399
-Yeah.
-And then, of course, COVID hit.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:42.735
And everyone was just
ground to a halt.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:47.573
But I did a concert
in Paris recently

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:49.742
in front of 20,000 people.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:53.579
And I haven't played a concert
in front of that kind of crowd

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:55.748
since March the 7th, 2020.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.083
And it felt really good.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:59.118
And, you know, I love my fans
and I want to go out

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:00.886
and give them
the best thing possible,

00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:03.756
and you know, I can't wait.
-Yeah.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:06.258
For a lot of people, this will
be their first concert back.

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:08.094
I mean, if you go
to eltonjohn.com,

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:11.097
if you want to see Elton,
you're coming to New York,

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:14.099
February 22nd and 23rd
at the Garden.

00:02:14.099 --> 00:02:15.435
Madison Square Garden.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:17.437
You're also playing
Barclays Center in March.

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:20.439
But Madison Square Garden
and Elton John go together

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:23.109
like peanut butter and jelly.

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.612
I mean, it's the greatest
combination.

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:28.447
We -- New Yorkers love you.

00:02:28.447 --> 00:02:31.451
-Well, you know,
I have to say New York is,

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:33.119
Madison Square Garden
in particular

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:34.787
is the finest place to play
in the world.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.289
I mean, you get really excited.

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:38.290
You never lose the excitement
of going backstage

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:40.293
and playing to that crowd.

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.128
I've done so many memorable
concerts there.

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.630
I played my 60th birthday
concert there,

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:47.133
the concert for 9/11.
-Yeah.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:50.303
-And there's something about
that New York crowd

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:52.471
that's just quite astonishing.

00:02:52.471 --> 00:02:55.475
And I've never done a show
at Madison Square Garden

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:58.644
where I didn't think --
it didn't do well.

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:00.813
And, you know,
it's a magic place.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.481
I'm so glad they never moved it.

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:04.817
Because if they'd have moved it,
the atmosphere would have gone.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.318
It's just a magic place.

00:03:06.318 --> 00:03:07.820
-Yeah, the house
has good bones, yeah.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.489
-It's great in New York because
New York's a magic place

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:13.493
and you got the best show in
the world right in front of you.

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:14.993
[ Applause ]

00:03:14.993 --> 00:03:18.063
-I want to ask you --
I've always wanted to ask you

00:03:18.063 --> 00:03:20.399
this story about -- 'cause
I've always heard this story,

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:24.404
but about John Lennon performing
with you at the Garden.

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.239
He -- This is post-Beatles.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.740
I think, actually,

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.576
it might've been the last time
he played live.

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:31.910
-It was.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:35.581
-You had a bet with John.

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:37.082
-Yeah, well,
I played on John's record

00:03:37.082 --> 00:03:39.751
"Whatever Gets You Thru
the Night," and sang on it too.

00:03:39.751 --> 00:03:42.088
And I said, "Okay, if this
record gets to number one,

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:44.089
you've got to come on,
play live with them."

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:45.591
And he said, "Okay, you're on."

00:03:45.591 --> 00:03:47.760
And by Jove,
it did get to number one,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.997
and then he had to keep
his promise, which he did,

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:54.333
at Madison Square Garden
on Thanksgiving.

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:56.669
And it was one of the most
magical moments in my life.

00:03:56.669 --> 00:04:00.873
Probably for me, the memory of
him coming onstage

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.908
and getting so much applause,

00:04:02.908 --> 00:04:05.745
I think all the band, and
myself, were moved to tears.

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:07.580
And it was such
a wonderful occasion.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.082
I don't think
he'd played in New York

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.750
since the Beatles
at Shea Stadium.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.252
-Yeah, that's correct.
-And it just --

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:16.923
You know, it was just
a magical moment in one's life

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:20.927
to see someone so loved
getting that so much acclaim.

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.762
And, you know, I had
such a great time with John

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:24.263
for two years,

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:28.100
and it's one of the highlights
of my life and my career.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.603
-I can't wait to see you
when you come back around.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:32.871
I will be screaming
from the crowd.

00:04:32.871 --> 00:04:34.707
I love you.
Elton John, everybody.

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:37.577
"The Lockdown Sessions"
is available now.

